From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:19:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Implement the last three runtime classes Office asks for.

ProtectionPolicyManager answers for Windows Information Protection, a policy an
administrator pushes to a managed device.  No such policy is in force here and
there is no channel through which one could arrive, so every question about one
has the answer it has on any unmanaged Windows machine: no identity is managed,
protection is off, enforcement is at NoProtection, access is Allowed.  That is
the answer, not a placeholder -- saying Blocked would have Word, Excel and the
WebView2 host withhold a file no policy asked them to withhold.  The access
requests hand back an operation that is already complete, so a caller that
awaits one is not left waiting on a policy engine that does not exist.
ProtectionPolicyAuditInfo and ThreadNetworkContext come with it; the audit
record is a settings object and round-trips.

UserActivityRequestManager is how an application offers to describe what the
user is doing so the shell can put it in Timeline.  Nothing here asks.  The
manager exists, a handler is registered and given a token it can unregister
with, and the event never fires -- which is what happens on a Windows machine
with the feature off.  Existing matters on its own: an application asks for
this class to find out whether the feature is available, and the answer to that
is not an activation failure.

AddPackageOptions is a bag of settings for PackageManager.  The flags and the
stub-package choice are values a caller sets and reads back, so they are
implemented and round-trip; the four collection members need vectors over types
from namespaces that are not here and say so.

Every IID is from the published metadata and was checked against Office's own
binaries on the build this prefix runs.  tools/winrtprobe covers all three:
85 of 85 checks pass against that prefix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b843f8e53b0c80efb5cba21dd9d2744ce643c353)

